WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.794
Ruud runs a metalworking shop and wants 60 kilowatts of solar.

2
00:00:04.794 --> 00:00:07.841
His installer says the grid has no capacity.

3
00:00:07.841 --> 00:00:14.050
Nobody can tell him whether that's true, for how long, or what he can do instead.

4
00:00:14.050 --> 00:00:18.550
GridQueue answers from what the grid operator has published.

5
00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:20.785
Same address, two answers.

6
00:00:20.785 --> 00:00:23.054
Feed-in: waiting list only.

7
00:00:23.054 --> 00:00:27.004
Consumption: 250 kilowatts stated as available.

8
00:00:27.004 --> 00:00:32.131
Capacity has a direction, and most tools never ask which one.

9
00:00:32.131 --> 00:00:38.110
Every answer is grounded in official grid operator publications.

10
00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:48.461
The date is Q3 2028, and the chip says non-binding, because the operator's own sentence says so.

11
00:00:48.461 --> 00:00:52.358
A codeerprognose is an estimate, not a promise.

12
00:00:52.358 --> 00:00:57.270
Every date carries its quote, its source and a hash.

13
00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:01.851
No firm capacity is not the end.

14
00:01:01.851 --> 00:01:08.316
The operator offers a non-firm connection up to 60 kilowatts, and congestion management.

15
00:01:08.316 --> 00:01:12.590
Each route is quoted, ranked, with who to contact.

16
00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:24.869
And for this postcode, it says: we could not establish an official position for this location and direction.

17
00:01:24.869 --> 00:01:26.213
We will not guess.

18
00:01:26.213 --> 00:01:32.790
Instead, it gives you the question to ask the operator, in their own vocabulary.

19
00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:39.987
Tavily searches only the operator's own site.

20
00:01:39.987 --> 00:01:46.044
Nemotron Ultra on Nebius Token Factory proposes claims as structured output.

21
00:01:46.044 --> 00:01:55.650
Then a gate in plain Python, with no model, checks every quote, date and kilowatt figure against the source text.

22
00:01:56.200 --> 00:02:05.339
Verified status: live runtime calls to Tavily and Nebius Token Factory query official operator documents, recorded to the ledger.

23
00:02:05.339 --> 00:02:08.314
The application pack re-checks every hash.

24
00:02:08.314 --> 00:02:12.740
Inject one unsupported date, and the pack is withheld.

25
00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:22.676
On a synthetic set we wrote ourselves: with the gate off, 10 fabricated dates reached the answer.

26
00:02:22.676 --> 00:02:23.871
With it on, 0.

27
00:02:23.871 --> 00:02:29.246
21 of 21 fabricated values blocked, all 10 genuine values kept.

28
00:02:29.246 --> 00:02:33.600
But 4 of 5 misattributed values got through.

29
00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:39.964
It reports published positions, not grid physics.

30
00:02:39.964 --> 00:02:46.300
Indicative dates stay non-binding, verified against official operator publications.

31
00:02:46.300 --> 00:02:49.150
It will not invent a date.
